.TH XUR.STD.RE 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.re \- Xur's reverse engineering standard library module
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::re
is a toolkit for binary analysis, live process interaction, machine code
disassembly, and .NET assembly manipulation. Each capability is backed by
a dedicated Rust crate and exposed as a submodule.
.SH MODULES
.SS std::re (top level) \(em binary images via pewter
Parse and construct PE and ELF binaries.
.TP
.B AnyImage::open(path)
Open a PE or ELF file from disk; returns a parsed image.
.TP
.B AnyImage::load(bytes)
Parse a binary image from a byte buffer.
.PP
Top-level also exposes export/import types:
.BR ExportEntry ,
.BR ExportLocation ,
.BR ImportEntry .
.SS std::re::pe \(em PE files via pewter
Direct access to PE structures and construction of new PE images.
.TP
.B PEFile::open(path)
Open a PE file. Fields such as
.BR coff_header ,
.BR optional_header ,
.BR sections ,
.BR imports ,
.B exports
are available through facet shapes.
.TP
.B ImageDef::new_dll(machine)
.TQ
.B ImageDef::new_exe(machine)
Start building a new PE image.
.TP
.B section_flags(names)
Convert a list of flag name strings to a section flags value.
.SS std::re::elf \(em ELF files via pewter
Access to ELF structures:
.BR ElfFile::open(path) ,
header fields, sections, segments, symbols.
.SS std::re::proc \(em live processes via procodile
Attach to and interact with running processes.
.TP
.B open(pid, access)
Open a process handle.
.I access
is one of
.BR \(dqread\(dq ,
.BR \(dqwrite\(dq ,
or
.BR \(dqall\(dq .
.TP
.B handle.modules()
List loaded modules (name, base address, size).
.TP
.B handle.read(address, size)
Read bytes from process memory.
.TP
.B handle.write(address, bytes)
Write bytes to process memory.
.TP
.B handle.inject(dll_path)
Inject a DLL into the target process (requires the
.B inject
feature).
.SS std::re::asm::x86 \(em x86 disassembly via iced\-x86
Decode and format x86/x64 machine code.
.TP
.B decode(bitness, bytes, ip)
Disassemble
.I bytes
at virtual address
.IR ip .
.I bitness
is 16, 32, or 64.
Returns a list of instruction objects with fields:
.BR ip ,
.BR len ,
.BR mnemonic ,
.BR op_count ,
and formatting methods.
.TP
.B encode(bitness, instructions, ip)
Assemble a list of instructions back to bytes.
.SS std::re::dotnet \(em .NET assemblies via hao
Read, construct, and write .NET (ECMA-335) assemblies.
.SS std::re::dotnet::il2cpp \(em Unity Il2Cpp games via hao\-il2cpp
Read type metadata from Unity Il2Cpp games and generate .NET proxy assemblies.
.TP
.B il2cpp::open(path)
Open a game folder. Returns a
.B Game
with
.BR types() ,
.BR find_type() ,
.BR write_assemblies() .
.SS std::re::dotnet::runtime \(em .NET runtime hosting via hao\-runtime
Start a .NET runtime (CoreCLR) and call into managed code.
.TP
.B runtime::coreclr()
Start or get the running CoreCLR. Returns a
.B Runtime
with
.BR load_assembly() ,
.BR function_pointer() ,
.BR method_pointer() .
.PP
.I Reading:
.TP
.B open(path)
Open a .NET assembly file from disk.
.TP
.B parse(bytes)
Parse a .NET assembly from a byte buffer.
.TP
.B module.all_types()
List all type definitions. Each type has
.BR name ,
.BR namespace ,
.BR methods ,
.BR fields .
.TP
.B module.to_csharp()
Decompile the module to a C# string representation.
.PP
.I Construction:
.TP
.B new(name, kind)
Create a new module.
.I kind
is
.B \(dqconsole\(dq
or
.BR \(dqdll\(dq .
.TP
.B module.add_assembly_ref(name)
Add a reference to an external assembly.
.TP
.B module.import_method(asm, type, name, sig)
Import a method from an assembly reference. Returns a member token.
.TP
.B module.corlib_type(ns, name)
Get a type reference from the core library.
.TP
.B module.add_type(typedef)
Add a constructed type definition to the module.
.TP
.B module.set_entry_point(method)
Set the module's entry point method.
.TP
.B module.write()
Serialize the module to bytes.
.TP
.B static_class(module, ns, name)
Create a new static class type definition.
.TP
.B public_static_method(name, sig, body)
Create a new public static method with the given signature and IL body.
.TP
.B add_method(typedef, method)
Add a method to a type definition, returning a method token.
.PP
.I Type and method signatures (\fBdotnet::sig\fR):
.TP
.B void(), bool(), char(), int32(), int64(), float64(), string(), object(), intptr()
Primitive type signatures.
.TP
.B sz_array(elem)
Single-dimension zero-based array of
.IR elem .
.TP
.B method_static(ret, params)
.TQ
.B method_instance(ret, params)
Method signatures, taking a return type and a list of parameter types.
.PP
.I IL emitter (\fBdotnet::il\fR):
.TP
.B emitter()
Create a new IL emitter.
.TP
.B e.ldstr(s), e.call(token), e.callvirt(token), e.newobj(token)
Load a string literal, call a method, virtual call, or constructor call.
.TP
.B e.ldc_i4(n), e.ldarg(n), e.ldloc(n), e.stloc(n)
Load an integer constant, load an argument, load/store a local.
.TP
.B e.ret(), e.pop(), e.dup(), e.ldnull()
Return, pop, duplicate, or load null.
.TP
.B e.finish()
Finalise the emitter and return a method body.
.SH EXAMPLES
Disassemble bytes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::re::asm::x86;

fn main() {
    let code = b"\\x55\\x48\\x89\\xe5";
    for insn in x86::decode(64, code, 0x1000) {
        io::println("{}", insn);
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read a .NET assembly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::re::dotnet;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let module = dotnet::open("Game.dll")?;
    for ty in module.all_types() {
        io::println("{}.{}", ty.namespace, ty.name);
    }
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Construct a .NET console app:
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::re::dotnet;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let sig = dotnet::sig;
    let module = dotnet::new("Hello", "console");
    module.add_assembly_ref("System.Console");
    let wl = module.import_method(
        "System.Console", "System.Console",
        "WriteLine",
        sig::method_static(sig::void(), [sig::string()])
    )?;
    let body = {
        let e = dotnet::il::emitter();
        e.ldstr("Hello from Xur!");
        e.call(wl);
        e.ldc_i4(0);
        e.ret();
        e.finish()
    };
    let main_sig = sig::method_static(
        sig::int32(),
        [sig::sz_array(sig::string())]
    );
    let m = dotnet::public_static_method("Main", main_sig, body);
    let prog = dotnet::static_class(module, "Hello", "Program");
    let entry = dotnet::add_method(prog, m);
    module.add_type(prog);
    module.set_entry_point(entry);
    std::fs::write_bytes("hello.dll", module.write()?);
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.RE
